            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "This Rossby wave train is a key explanation for the occurrence of the Pacific South American Pattern (PSA), which is a winter-dominated pattern of troughs and ridges that connects ENSO variability in the tropical Pacific with West Antarctica and the Antarctic Peninsula [123] and in particular, the depth of the ASL [117, 119].",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
